OpenCL handover timing - the two handovers of ofxGPURender.h on one 1080p frame

Machine : Windows 10.0.19045, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060, OpenCL 3.0 CUDA (NVIDIA platform)
Build   : templates/minimal-opencl-ofx/test/run-tests.bat, MSVC Release, bundle rebuilt from
          an empty build/ directory in this session; the timed section is in
          templates/minimal-opencl-ofx/test/opencl_suite.cpp ("[8/9] the two handovers at
          1080p, timed"), reached through the suite's --frames argument
Command : opencl_suite <bundle>/Contents/Win64/OpenCLGain.ofx --frames N

Result  : images (image2d_t) is slower than buffers (cl_mem) in every one of the 16 paired
          runs kept here - median 12.50 vs 13.61 ms/frame at 300 frames (+8.9%) and 13.66
          vs 14.75 at 120 frames (+8.0%). A hidden full-frame copy would cost a multiple,
          not a tenth, so image2d_t is neither the fast path nor a disguised copy on this
          driver: it is the slightly slower of the two.
          What the span contains: the whole FakeHost::render() round trip - the plug-in's
          enqueue, the host's clFinish, and the blocking readback of 33.2 MB - so these are
          not kernel-only figures and must not be read against the CUDA rows in
          references/runtime-comparison.md section 3 (0.20-0.31 ms, frame resident).

